# L0b: an all-four reset with the heal, then the first four-card attach of the LANES profile (D0's one-user 16-row block beside M3,
# the lane admission and the lane gate, c2-packed-tp4-lanes-gate) with a short smoke: a warmup and one coding stream. The cheapest
# step that pays for D0's first four-card attach - the M=16 programs, the second block's trace region, the collectives handed to the
# solo block's publication warm - so a failure there stops the window before L1's three long arms, and is paid once, not in d0-solo
# and again in lanes-mixed. The smoke's stream is a lone standard request (no fast mark), so no solo round runs here: the fast lane's
# rounds are L1's. Read: the ready line; the launched-argv line (profile c2-packed-tp4-lanes-gate, QWEN_FAST_TP=4); "[LANE] engaged";
# the B6 publication warm's warmed line for the solo block as well as M3 (a "skipped reason=no-collectives" is the failure the
# collectives fix removed); every packed-any admission UNQUALIFIED line (only the pending evidence sections are expected); the
# "dram after attach" line, whose headroom must leave the per-request engines their captures; coherent text in coding.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env
# on a throwaway commit of tp4/lanes and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image L0 builds from this same commit.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min (heal up to 3 more); the engine build 10-30 min (D0's M=16 programs compile the first time);
# the two tests 3-8 min: 15-45 min in all.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lanes-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-lanes-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding
